<!--
  Power profile for the Ulefone Armor 29 Pro (GQ5012BF1, MT6878).

  Replaces the vendor placeholder (generic MediaTek values: 3/4 CPU speeds per
  cluster that this SoC does not have, all modem values 0, capacity 21200),
  which left CPU, mobile radio and Wi-Fi out of Battery usage.

  Units: mA in the fuel gauge's (sh366003) units = single-cell equivalent at
  ~3.85 V, the same units Android uses for capacity and drain on this phone.
  All values measured on the phone 2026-11-15/16 from the battery gauge
  (24-50 samples per point, median), screen off and CPU pinned to minimum
  unless noted. Runs 2-5 were done with USB connected and the charger power
  path off (/sys/devices/platform/charger/enable_power_path=0); a repeat of
  run-1 CPU points that way matched (big 125 vs 127, little 12.3 vs 13 mA).

  cpu.core_power.*  per-core increment, 1 vs 2 busy cores per frequency,
                    fitted a*f + b*f^3 (little 2.28/1.26, big 20.10/4.06)
  cpu.cluster_power / cpu.active   1-core minus 2-core increment (~1 mA)
  cpu.idle          awake idle (82.5) minus the suspend floor
  cpu.suspend       overnight screen-off drain (5 % of 8874 mAh in 9.9 h,
                    1 % awake) minus modem sleep
  screen.on         screen on at minimum brightness vs off: 37
  screen.full       OLED (Visionox VTDR6115): brightness cost depends on
                    content. Min->max (slider 100 %, backlight 2049) was +14
                    on the dark lock screen and +127 with colour inversion.
                    Value is for typical mixed content (APL ~0.3); full white
                    would be ~150-300.  ESTIMATE from measured endpoints.
  gps.on            GPS tracking with fix vs off, 3 cycles: 21.5
  wifi.*            connected idle +2, scanning +25, download at ~89 Mbit/s
                    +91 after CPU; controller rx/tx scaled to the chip's own
                    reported rx/tx airtime during that download (29 % / 13 %)
  modem             airplane vs registered idle +2 (sleep); connected tail
                    after a small request +10 for ~6 s (idle); LTE download at
                    ~53 Mbit/s +126 after CPU (receive). The modem reports no
                    TX time, so transmit = receive (not measured separately).
  radio.active      call power = LTE active (VoLTE), not measured on a call.
  NOT MEASURED (vendor values kept): ambient, bluetooth, audio, video, camera,
  radio.scanning, radio.on.
-->
